  "setting": "Parents' narrow tube house (nhà ống) with a ground-floor shop in a lane in Đống Đa, Hanoi, until 2008",
  "turns": [
    {"turnId": 1, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "Where was it?"},
    {"turnId": 2, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "Hanoi. A small lane in Đống Đa district. My parents' house, we lived there until about 2008. It was a nhà ống, a tube house. Very narrow at the front, maybe four metres, and then it just goes back and back, twenty metres or so."},
    {"turnId": 3, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "How did you go in?"},
    {"turnId": 4, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "Through the big folding metal door at the front, the cửa xếp, the kind you pull across. In the day it was open all the way and the front room was my mother's little shop, she had a glass counter there. At night the motorbikes came inside, three of them, parked in that front room."},
    {"turnId": 5, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "And behind the shop?"},
    {"turnId": 6, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "The stairs. Steep, concrete, against the left wall. Wait, you mean standing outside looking in? Then the right. The right wall. And past the stairs the kitchen, quite dark, a gas stove on a tiled counter."},
    {"turnId": 7, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "Was there any light back there?"},
    {"turnId": 8, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "There was the giếng trời, the sky well, a small open square past the kitchen that went all the way up through the house, so the rain came straight down into it. The water tank was in there, a big blue plastic one. No, the blue one was up on the roof. Down in the sky well it was a cement tank. And my grandmother's lime tree in a pot."},
    {"turnId": 9, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "And the bathroom?"},
    {"turnId": 10, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "Right at the very back, behind the sky well. Tiny, just a squat toilet. You had to go past the kitchen and the sky well in the dark to pee at night. I hated that."},
    {"turnId": 11, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "Upstairs?"},
    {"turnId": 12, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "On the second floor, my parents' bedroom at the front, with a door out to the balcony over the street. Lane, I mean, it was only a lane. And my brother and me in the back room. Between them just a little landing where the stairs came up."},
    {"turnId": 13, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "And above that?"},
    {"turnId": 14, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "Third floor was the altar room, the phòng thờ, at the front, with the bàn thờ, the ancestors' altar, and the photos of my grandfather and his parents. Behind it, the door out to the roof, the sân thượng, the flat terrace. My dad kept his birds up there in cages."},
    {"turnId": 15, "speaker": "B", "transcript": "How high were the floors?"},
    {"turnId": 16, "speaker": "A", "transcript": "The ground floor was high, the shop room maybe three and a half metres, because of the shop. Upstairs less. I don't really know."}
  ],
